  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Myanmar project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgtIn accordance with the respondents and the field staff, there are unmet and urgent needs of humanitarian assistance for conflict and displaced people. Therefore, Family World would like to assist and cover who are people in need and where hard to reach areas in Hakha, Falam, and Matupi townships, Chin state. This urgent humanitarian assistance will respond to the conflict affected groups ofltbgtltigt 5040 affected&#xa0;people (520&#xa0;men, 573&#xa0;women, 532&#xa0;boys, and 591girls in Hakha, 490 men, 551 women, 530 boys, 538 girls in Falam, 175&#xa0;men, 211women, 157&#xa0;boys, 172&#xa0;girls in Matupi) who are living at&#xa0;10&#xa0;villages/camps in Hakha, 6 villages/camps in Falam, and 10&#xa0;villages/camps in Matupi townships.lt/igtlt/bgt The project aims to provide multi-sectoral lifesaving support and assistance to conflict-affected populations. ltbrgtThe provision of immediate access through Education, Shelter/NFI, Protection, and Food intervention in three townships, Chin state. In Matupi township, there is intervention from 2023 First Standard Allocation (CBPF-MM-23-S-NGO-25677), however there are still those who urgently need to cover for conflict and affected people. The project targets are hard-to-reach conflict areas and under-served locations through a multi-sectoral assistance. And this project will improve the overall wellbeing and the dignity and the conditions of conflict affected women, girls, men, boys, and persons with disabilities. Additionally, the project will directly assist 1410&#xa0;affected&#xa0;children by Education intervention, 664&#xa0;households by Shelters reconstruction, and 5040&#xa0;displaced people by NFI intervention, 1410&#xa0;displaced children&#xa0;by Protection, and 5040&#xa0;conflict&#xa0;displaced people by Food intervention as targeted. The project will engage community and promote, both men, women, boys, and girls, including persons with disabilities, single moms, and elderly persons through activities on mainstreaming Education, Protection, Shelters and NFIs, and Food Security.&#xa0;ltbrgtFamily World is an established organization in Chin state with a strong experience of more than 10 years in Humanitarian Aid and Rural Development. There are part-time volunteers, enthusiastic staff, who can contribute a great deal of help in implementation of this project timely and fairly. Thus, Family World is aiming to achieve this intervention accordingly in the project period.&#xa0;ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
